From eab3468d0c4fcbf1982971900528fd9361297a93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:57:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SPU: run only the sound channels that are due, NEON mixer
 sums, direct main RAM for sound DMA, capture and DMA

FastMix (SPU::SetFastMix, off by default here; exact): a channel's output only changes when its timer
overflows, when its registers are written or when it stops, so Mix keeps each channel's output and panned terms
and the Mix at which it next takes a sample, runs only the channels due (all of them after any SPU register
write), and returns the last sums when none is due; the skipped Mixes' cycles are added to the timers before
the channel runs again or the state is saved. A due channel's samples are taken by Run's loop without its
checks (RunValid). The mixers sum the 16 channels' terms with NEON. Sound DMA bursts and capture flushes in main
RAM skip ARM7Read32/ARM7Write32's dispatch (the JIT check stays), and a capture with no sample due only adds
its cycles. Not with interpolation, and DS only for the memory shortcuts.

FastDMA (NDS::SetFastDMA, off by default; exact, DS only): 32-bit DMA from main RAM to the GX FIFO goes
straight to GPU3D::Write32 (as FastGXDMA), and between main RAM addresses straight to MainRAM after the JIT's
check; the ARM9's main RAM -> fixed destination timing is UnitTimings9_32's MRAM burst table lookup, chosen once
per run instead of per unit.
